entry.summary:
Every major applicant tracking system publishes its job board as a public JSON What isn't documented is what happens once you actually try to read all of them 200 OK while These are the five that cost me real time. All of them are verifiable with curl, no authentication, no account. limit at 20 — and returns an empty array if you exceed it
Workday's job search is a POST, not a GET: POST https://${host}/wday/cxs/${tenant}/${site}/jobs Content-Type: application/json
{ "appliedFacets": {}, "limit": 20, "offset": 0, "searchText": "" }
The obvious optimization is to raise limit to cut the number of round trips. { "appliedFacets": {}, "limit": 100, "offset": 0, "searchText": "" }
You get 200 OK. You get a well-formed response body. And jobPostings is an empty array. No error. No warning. No…
